# Client ACLs are per-host, not the whole LAN subnet. Anything on
# 10.57.57.0/24 could previously mount every export below; combined with
# no_root_squash that meant any device in the house had root on the backup
# tree. Narrowed 2026-08-11 to the hosts that actually mount, verified
# against live nfsd peers first.
#
#   10.57.57.80        kubernetes-1 (on pve-1)
#   10.57.57.82        kubernetes-2 (on pve-2) — added 2026-09-04
#   10.57.57.83        kubernetes-3 (on pve-3) — added 2026-09-04
#
# .81 and .84 were dropped on 2026-09-04. They were a retired worker and a
# retired control plane; with no_root_squash, each was a standing root grant
# on the backup tree to whatever might take the address next.
#
# Adding a client means adding its IP here, not widening back to /24.
/media/library                  10.57.57.80(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.82(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.83(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash)
/media/backups                  10.57.57.80(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,crossmnt) 10.57.57.82(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,crossmnt) 10.57.57.83(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,crossmnt)
